# =============================================================================
# Durable AI Platform
# =============================================================================

# --- Instance parameter files: THESE CARRY CREDENTIALS -----------------------
# The --param-file inputs used when creating an instance contain the Cassandra
# superuser password in cleartext, so they are ignored by name.
#
# Commit templates instead. `*.example.json` is not ignored:
#   cassandra.example.json  ->  cp cassandra.example.json cassandra.json
cassandra.json
platform.json
*.params.json
params.json
!*.example.json

# --- Terraform / OpenTofu ----------------------------------------------------
# .terraform/ holds provider binaries. The lock file is ignored because these
# stacks run under OpenTofu on the platform side, where a lock pinned to a local
# build would not apply. Versions are pinned in each module's versions.tf.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.*
crash.log
crash.*.log
# Omnistrate manages Terraform state, so these should not exist. Ignored as a
# backstop in case someone runs a stack by hand.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
# Local variable files can carry DB passwords.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!example.tfvars

# --- Helm --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packaged chart artifacts. `local-artifacts/` is the destination the README
# suggests for the pre-packaged form of the ai-worker local chart artifact; the
# .tgz is a build output, not source.
local-artifacts/
*.tgz
images/ai-worker/chart/charts/
images/ai-worker/chart/Chart.lock

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Secrets and cloud credentials -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/templates/*.key
kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig
.omnistrate/
# GCP service-account JSON keys. Anything matching is a live credential.
# NOTE: gcloud names downloaded keys after the project, e.g.
# `my-project-1a2b3c4d5e6f.json`, which no safe pattern can catch without
# ignoring every .json in the repo. Move those outside the working tree; do not
# rely on this list to save you.
*sa-key.json
*sa_key.json
service-account*.json
gcp-credentials*.json
client_secret*.json

# --- Editors and OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.netrwhist

# --- Agent tooling -----------------------------------------------------------
# Local skill/agent setup, not part of the deliverable. `.claude/skills/*` are
# symlinks into `.agents/`, which would resolve wrongly for anyone cloning onto a
# different layout anyway.
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json

# --- Scratch -----------------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
*.log
!seed/*.log
